  {"page": 2, "blocks": [
   {"role": "heading", "text": "Why measurement error matters"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Every measurement has an uncertainty"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Random error: scatters readings around the true value"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Reduced by repeating the measurement"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Systematic error shifts all readings the same way"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Example: a thermometer that reads 1 degree high"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Fixed by calibration"},
   {"role": "list", "text": "Report results as value ± uncertainty"},
   {"role": "dropped", "text": "ENVS 101 · Lecture 4: Measurement"},
